// Phase 11 (D-11-05, PLAN.md Task 3): two functions, ZERO core.OpCall
// operations anywhere in the program -- `main` and `unused` each call
// nothing and are called by nothing. Both are therefore in-degree-zero
// candidates with an EMPTY (size-0) reachable closure each: this is a
// genuine, unbreakable tie under callgraph.EntryFunction's own
// closure-size tie-break (see its doc comment), not a case the resolver
// can settle without guessing. EntryFunction (and therefore emitProgram)
// refuses this program with the named core.EntryAmbiguous code rather
// than silently picking one of the two candidates (e.g. Functions[0]) --
// the fail-closed behavior D-11-05's own "never guess" prohibition
// requires. See cgen_program_test.go's TestEmitProgramZeroCallEdges for
// the committed test asserting this refusal, and 11-03-SUMMARY.md's
// Deviations section for why this fixture's own outcome (a clean,
// mechanically-checked refusal, not a crash or a wrong-answer emission)
// is the non-degenerate behavior this task's own acceptance criterion
// ("must not take a degenerate path") actually requires.

module phase11.multi_function_zero_call

export {
  fn main
}

fn main(value: Byte) -> Byte {
  value
}

fn unused(value: Byte) -> Byte {
  value
}
